PROLOGUE IMAGE PROMPT – ALUCARD: THE DEMON HUNTER (Extended, In-Depth)
Aspect Ratio: 9:16 vertical
Style Matrix: Neo-Ukiyo-e (modern reinterpretation of Edo-period woodblock prints) fused with traditional Sumi-e (ink wash painting) – featuring dynamic asymmetrical composition, negative space, bleeding ink textures, visible brush stroke directionality, and a muted yet dramatic palette of sumi blacks, parchment creams, oxidized silver, deep indigo, and restrained vermilion accents. The realism layer sits atop: hyperdetailed skin, fabric weave, metal patina, and environmental atmosphere rendered in 8K resolution with cinematic anamorphic characteristics.
Lighting & Camera: Master-quality ARRI Alexa 65 with anamorphic 85mm lens at f/1.8. Single dominant key light from upper-left (golden-hour warmth) feathered into a cool fill from the right (blue glow of gauntlet). Deep chiaroscuro shadows hugging the character's right side. Subtle lens flare at the edge of frame, not obscuring detail. Film grain applied (Kodak Vision3 500T emulation). Color grade: teal-and-amber split with lifted blacks, crushed shadows, and soft roll-off in highlights.
CENTRAL FIGURE – ALUCARD (Half-Body, Throne Pose)
Position & Posture: Alucard sits centered, slightly left-of-center to allow his greatsword to balance the right side. His body is angled three-quarter toward camera, head turned to meet the viewer's gaze directly. His right leg is crossed over his left, his gauntleted right hand resting on his knee. His left hand grips the arm of the throne loosely, fingers relaxed. His posture exudes exhausted royalty – a king of a forgotten battlefield. His spine is straight, shoulders back, chin slightly lifted, but there is a weight to his eyelids, a weariness in the set of his jaw.
Facial Details (Strictly from Data):
Hair: Dirty blonde, short, stylishly tousled, swept back and to the side in layered textured locks. A few strands fall forward over his forehead, catching the key light. The hair has visible individual strands, slight oil at the roots, natural variation from pale gold to deeper honey.
Eyes: Piercing icy blue. Irises show radial fibers, a dark limbal ring, and a faint internal glow – not supernatural but reflective of the gauntlet's light. His gaze is calm, confident, but with a micro-expression of melancholy. Visible lower eyelid crease, natural dark circles from sleep deprivation.
Skin: Fair pale ivory. Subsurface scattering visible on the bridge of the nose, cheekbones, and the tips of his ears. Peach fuzz on upper lip and cheeks (very fine, only visible at 8K). A small, faded scar on his left jawline – not in the original data but added for realism, can be omitted if you prefer absolute purity. I will keep it subtle and removable.
Jawline & Nose: Sharp aristocratic jawline, straight prominent nose. The jaw casts a shadow onto his neck. His Adam's apple is visible but not exaggerated.
Expression: Neutral but authoritative. No smile, no frown. His mouth is slightly parted as if about to speak.
Clothing & Armor (Strict Adherence):
Coat: Deep navy blue and cerulean high-collared long-tailed duster coat with bronze antique gold trim along the edges. The coat is open at the front, revealing the dark double-breasted vest beneath. The fabric is a heavy wool blend, showing micro-texture, slight nap, and a few loose threads. The collar is flipped up at the back but folded down at the front.
Vest: Dark double-breasted vest fastened with silver-toned hexagonal buttons. The vest fits snugly, hinting at his lean athletic physique. Buttons have a brushed metal finish.
Brooch: Stylized silver-winged brooch pinned to his right lapel. The brooch glows with a soft internal azure light – this glow is subtle, not overpowering, like bioluminescence. The wings are detailed with individual feather-like engravings.
Gloves & Gauntlet (Critical):
Left hand: Simple dark leather glove with a wide blue cuff. The leather is worn, with creases at the knuckles and wrist.
Right arm (gauntlet): Heavy segmented silver gauntlet covering from shoulder to fingers. The segments overlap like dragon scales, each etched with runic conduits glowing faint blue. The gauntlet has visible rivets, slight oxidation at the joints, and a matte finish contrasted with polished highlights. The fingers are articulated, each segment moving independently. The blue glow emanates from the recessed channels, not from the surface – it appears as cold light bleeding through gaps.
Lower Body (visible partially): Form-fitting dark charcoal trousers, tucked into sturdy knee-high black leather combat boots with horizontal straps and silver buckles at the ankles. Only the left boot is visible (right leg crossed), showing the buckle detail and the leather's grain.
Coat tails: The long tails of the duster coat flare out behind him over the throne's arms, lined with tan light brown fabric. They drape like a cape, catching the fill light.
The Throne:
Constructed from fused materials – jagged black iron, petrified demon bones (ribs forming the backrest), and broken silver chains hanging like macabre tassels. The seat is worn velvet in deep burgundy, now faded and torn.
The throne sits on a raised dais of cracked stone, overgrown with ghostly white lichen (ink-wash style).
The left arm of the throne has a carved wolf's head motif; the right arm (where Alucard's gauntleted hand rests) has a smaller skull similar to his sword's hilt.
The Greatsword:
Placed vertically on the right side of the throne, point down, hilt at Alucard's shoulder height.
The blade: Single-edged, colossal, nearly as tall as Alucard. The cutting edge is clean silver; the spine has bone-like serrations. A recessed channel runs down the center glowing with intense supernatural blue energy that pulses like a heartbeat.
The hilt: Silver-carved skull with glowing blue eye sockets, framed by jagged wing-like protrusions as a crossguard.
The blade's glow casts blue reflections onto Alucard's coat and the right side of his face.
BACKGROUND – AFTER-IMAGES (Ink Wash Battle Stances)
Surrounding Alucard in a semicircular halo are three translucent full-body after-images rendered in sumi-e brush stroke style with varying opacities (30% to 60%). Each after-image maintains identical character design – same hair, coat, gauntlet, sword – only the pose and energy effects differ. The after-images bleed into the dark ink background as if painted with wet brush on rice paper, with visible brush direction and ink blooms.
After-Image #1 (Left – Mid-Whirling Smash):
