Energy: The explosion is half sumi ink splash (black and deep indigo) and half radiant light. Small motes of blue energy drift outward like falling stars.
Scale: Larger than Alucard, positioned above his head, serving as a crown-like halo.
Additional Ink Elements:
Drifting blue embers (small circular ink blooms with bright centers) float randomly.
A flock of ink-washed crows or shadow-birds (symbolizing demons) recede into the dark background.
The ground beneath the throne has subtle ink pooling suggesting blood or shadow.
LOWER SECTION – TYPOGRAPHY, TAGLINE, DIALOGUE & LOGO
A horizontal band across the bottom 20% of the image, simulating aged parchment with deckled edges, ink bleed, and slight water damage. The band is not a perfect rectangle; it has irregular edges that blend into the dark sumi background.
Calligraphy Title (Sosho & Reisho Influence):
ALUCARD in large vertical brushed Latin letters, each character formed with sosho (cursive grass script) energy – bold, sweeping strokes with visible speed variations and ink splatter. The letters are silver-gray with a subtle blue glow.
Below, in smaller reisho (clerical script) horizontal: — THE DEMON HUNTER — in crisp, structured brush strokes, dark charcoal ink.
Main Tagline:
"The Weight of a Name"
Rendered in semi-cursive gyosho, medium size, placed below the title but above the dialogue. Ink color: faded vermilion (red-brown).
Dialogue (Ink Cartouche):
The dialogue is enclosed in a traditional Japanese-style cartouche – a rectangular frame with rounded corners, made of brushed ink lines, slightly irregular.
Text: "The empire remembers my father as a fool. I remember him as a hero. One of these memories will outlive the other, and I intend to make certain it is mine."
Font style: Simulated hand-brushed Latin script, elegant but with grit. The text is white with a subtle drop shadow, set against a semi-transparent dark background within the cartouche.
Logo / Seal (User Provided – Integrated with Character):
Placement: The logo will be placed in two ways as per "bent with the character":
Primary: A large ink-stamp seal (hanko-style) in the lower right corner of the image, overlapping the parchment band and slightly bleeding into the dark background. The seal is circular, deep crimson red (vermilion), with the logo's emblem carved in white negative space. Around the seal, a faint ink bloom (water spreading outward).
Secondary (Subtle Integration): The same logo emblem is faintly etched into the throne's backrest, near Alucard's left shoulder – as if branded into the metal. This echo ties the logo to the character himself.
