PANEL 7 (Bottom, wide, cinematic – 30% height): The aftermath. Dawn. Alucard sits on a rocky outcrop overlooking a valley. His horse grazes nearby. His face is bruised, tear-streaked, but his eyes are hardening into the cold gaze of an adult. Behind him, the sun rises over the mountains, but the horizon still smokes from the battle. He holds his mother's sketch in one hand and a broken piece of Second Regiment banner in the other. Caption in bold handwritten font across the bottom: "The Second Regiment was destroyed that night. Commander Arton's body was never recovered – a detail the empire's official records cite as proof of his 'desertion.' Alucard would spend the rest of his life proving them wrong." No dialogue. The final image fades into sumi ink wash effect at the edges, transitioning from realistic to brush-stroke as the chapter ends.

