PANEL 5 (Small, action – 10% height): A close-up on Alucard's hands (age 14) gripping a wooden training sword. His knuckles are bloody, wrapped in fraying cloth. A piece of folded parchment is tucked into his belt – a handwritten note. The note is partially visible, with Tigreal's distinctive handwriting: "Your father was a hero. Never forget." Caption beside the note: "He left notes in Alucard's quarters – tactical observations, corrections to his form, occasional words of encouragement that never quite crossed into warmth." No speech bubble.

PANEL 6 (Large, emotional turning point – 25% height): The Monastery's rooftop under a starry sky. Alucard (age 15) sits alone, looking out over the mountains. Tigreal sits beside him – this is the first time they are shown together, face to face, without shadows. Tigreal's face is kind but sad, his armor simplified, his Moniyan badge hidden. Alucard's expression is conflicted – angry but desperate for connection. Dialogue bubble from Tigreal (soft, measured): "I served with your father. He was my closest friend. And he did not disobey orders – he was betrayed." Alucard's bubble (voice cracking, years of suppressed grief breaking through): "Why didn't you tell me before?" Tigreal's bubble: "Because you were a child. And the truth would have destroyed you before you were strong enough to carry it." Long pause. No dialogue. Caption at bottom of panel: "That knowledge, more than any technique, became the foundation upon which Alucard built himself."

PANEL 7 (Small, montage – 8% height): A vertical strip of three small vignettes showing Alucard's progression through the Monastery years: (top) age 12 running laps in snow, exhausted; (middle) age 14 sparring with three opponents at once, holding his own; (bottom) age 16 standing in full training armor, alone in the center of the yard, sword planted, his face now cold, controlled, the haunted child replaced by a disciplined young man. No dialogue. Caption running alongside the vignettes: "He trained with a ferocity that bordered on self-destruction, pushing his body past its limits again and again, as if he believed that physical exhaustion might somehow silence the screaming in his mind."

PANEL 8 (Bottom, wide, cinematic – 20% height): The Monastery gates at dawn. Snow is falling. Alucard (age 16, final year as novice) stands at the gate, looking out toward the south – toward the Barren Lands, toward the demons, toward his future. He wears his first set of real armor – simple steel breastplate over dark blue tunic, no gauntlet yet, but his stance is already that of a hunter. Tigreal stands behind him, at a distance, hand raised in a silent farewell. The rising sun casts long shadows. Caption in bold handwritten font across the bottom: "Tigreal could not tell Alucard the whole truth. Not yet. So instead, he taught – how to read an opponent's intent, how to conserve energy, how to turn an enemy's momentum against them. And in his own quiet way, he taught Alucard that his father had been a hero." Final line of caption, larger: "That knowledge became the weapon the Monastery could never give him."

SPEECH BUBBLE STYLE NOTES: Same as Chapter One – thin black outline, white fill with 85% opacity, dark charcoal text. Jagged edges for shouting, dashed outlines for whispers. Tails point to speaker's mouth. Narrative captions: rectangular boxes with semi-transparent dark background, white text, placed in corners or along edges, subtle drop shadow.

TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS FOR ENTIRE IMAGE: The 9:16 canvas (e.g., 1080x1920 pixels) contains these eight panels arranged vertically with narrow gutters (2-5 pixel black lines) separating them. Panel sizes as specified (percentage of height). All characters must be identical from panel to panel – young Alucard ages consistently (hair length gradually increases, face sharpens, height grows), Tigreal remains consistent across his appearances. Lighting changes per scene (blizzard, candlelit dormitory, snowy training yard, night rooftop, dawn) but character colors remain accurate to descriptions. Hyperrealistic detail with ink wash background elements (sumi clouds, bleeding shadows) only in skies or deep backgrounds, never over characters. Skin shows pores, peach fuzz, scars, bruises where appropriate. Fabrics have visible weave, wear, stains. The final panel fades into sumi ink wash effect at the edges as the chapter ends, transitioning from realistic to brush-stroke.










