PANEL 8 (Medium, completion – 10% height): The gauntlet is fully fitted. Alucard sits on the table, his right arm now encased in segmented silver plates, glowing runes pulsing with a soft blue light. He is looking at his new hand, flexing the fingers – they move smoothly. His face is exhausted but there is a flicker of wonder, of relief. The Head Artificer stands back, wiping his brow, a rare smile on his weathered face. Speech bubble from Head Artificer (satisfied, but cautious): "It will hold. For now. But the corruption is not gone – only contained. You will need to maintain the gauntlet. The runes will fade. The alloys will crack. And every time you use the power, the darkness will spread a little further." Alucard's bubble (quiet, resolute): "It's enough. I'll make it enough."

PANEL 9 (Small, vertical – 5% height): A vignette: Tigreal standing in the workshop doorway, half-hidden in shadow. His face is visible – his eyes are sad, but he nods once, then turns and walks away. No dialogue. Caption: "Tigreal watched in silence. He knew what the gauntlet truly was – a cage, not a cure. But it was the only gift he could give."

PANEL 10 (Bottom, wide, cinematic – 12% height): Alucard standing alone in the Monastery courtyard at night. He is fully dressed – his navy and cerulean duster coat, his greatsword on his back, and the new gauntlet glowing faintly on his right arm. Snow is falling. He raises his gauntleted hand, looking at the blue light that seeps between the plates. His face is no longer that of a boy – it is the face of a hunter. In the distance, the Monastery gates are open, leading out to the Barren Lands. Caption in bold handwritten font across the bottom: "The gauntlet was a masterpiece of magical engineering. Alucard has never thought of it that way. To him, it is a cage – a beautifully crafted, exquisitely detailed cage that keeps the darkness in his arm from spreading to the rest of his body." Final line, italic: "He has two years, if the estimates are accurate. He intends to make every day count."

SPEECH BUBBLE STYLE NOTES: Same as previous chapters – thin black outline, white fill with 85% opacity, dark charcoal text. Jagged edges for shouting, dashed outlines for whispers. The High Priest's bubble uses a darker fill (70% opacity, tinged gold) to convey authority. Narrative captions: rectangular boxes with semi-transparent dark background, white text, placed in corners or along edges, subtle drop shadow. For this chapter, captions are minimal – the story is told through action and dialogue.

