CHARACTER APPEARANCE REFERENCES (strictly follow for every panel):

Alucard (age 18–20, after years of hunting with the gauntlet): Dirty blonde hair, tousled, swept back and to the side in layered textured locks – slightly longer than in earlier chapters, wind-worn. Piercing icy blue eyes that have grown colder, more distant, with a faint glow that mirrors the gauntlet's light. Sharp aristocratic jawline, straight prominent nose, fair pale ivory skin now showing slight weathering (windburn, small scars). Lean highly athletic warrior physique – broad shoulders, narrow waist, the body of a master fencer. Wears his full hunter gear: deep navy and cerulean high-collared long-tailed duster coat with bronze antique gold trim, dark double-breasted vest with silver-toned hexagonal buttons, stylized silver-winged brooch pinned to right lapel glowing with soft internal azure light. Mismatched armor: left hand covered by simple dark leather glove with wide blue cuff, right arm encased in heavy segmented silver gauntlet with glowing blue runic conduits. Dark charcoal trousers, sturdy knee-high black leather combat boots with horizontal straps and silver buckles. His greatsword is slung across his back or resting beside him – colossal single-edged blade with skull hilt and glowing blue channel.

No other characters appear in this chapter – it is a solo character study of Alucard. The "anatomy" is explored through close-ups, silhouettes, and contemplative moments.

PANEL 1 (Top, establishing wide shot – 15% of image height): A quiet forest clearing at dawn. Alucard stands alone in the center, his back to the viewer, looking out over a mist-covered valley. His greatsword is planted in the earth before him, both hands resting on the pommel. His coat tails flare slightly in a gentle wind. The sun is just rising behind the mountains, casting long shadows. The mood is peaceful but heavy. Caption in top-left corner, typewriter font: "To look at Alucard is to see a man carved from ice and fire. He stands just over six feet tall, with a physique that balances the broad-shouldered power of a warrior with the lean, coiled grace of a predator." No dialogue.

PANEL 2 (Medium, full body – 12% height): A side profile view of Alucard standing, slightly turned. The camera captures his entire body from head to boots. His posture is relaxed but ready – weight evenly distributed, center of gravity low, shoulders back. The gauntlet on his right arm glows faintly. His greatsword is visible over his shoulder. Caption below the panel: "His body is not bulky – he has never been interested in the kind of strength that comes from raw mass – but it is dense, packed with the kind of muscle that develops only through years of rigorous, disciplined training. His movements are economical, each gesture stripped of unnecessary flourish, as if he has calculated the exact amount of energy required for every action and refuses to waste a single erg."

PANEL 3 (Large, portrait – 20% of image height): A close-up of Alucard's face, straight-on, from the collarbones up. This is the definitive portrait of the hunter. His icy blue eyes hold the viewer, unblinking. The lighting is soft overcast – no harsh shadows, revealing every detail. His dirty blonde hair is slightly disheveled, strands falling over his forehead. The silver-winged brooch glows softly on his lapel, casting a faint blue light onto his jaw. Caption over the panel, split into two parts: "His face is the face of an aristocrat who has been forced to learn what lives in the dark. The jawline is sharp, angular – the kind of bone structure that artists love to sketch and enemies learn to fear. His cheekbones are high, casting shadows that make his eyes seem even deeper than they already are. His nose is straight, prominent – the nose of a man who has never had to justify his existence to anyone. His skin is pale – not the sickly pallor of illness, but the cool, ivory fairness of someone who has spent more time in shadow than in sunlight."

PANEL 4 (Small, extreme close-up – 8% height): A tight shot on Alucard's eyes – just the eyes and the bridge of his nose. The icy blue irises show radial fibers, a dark limbal ring, and a faint internal glow. There is no warmth in them, no softness. Instead, they hold something that looks, from this angle, like an abyss. Caption below: "It is his eyes, though, that unsettle people. They are a pale, icy blue, the colour of a winter sky just before a storm. There is no warmth in them, no softness, no hint of vulnerability. Instead, they hold something that looks, from certain angles, like an abyss – a depth that suggests Alucard has seen things that cannot be unseen, has done things that cannot be undone, and has made peace with all of it."

PANEL 5 (Medium, hands and gauntlet – 10% height): A detailed shot of Alucard's hands resting on his sword's pommel. The left hand wears a simple dark leather glove with a wide blue cuff – the leather is worn, creased at the knuckles. The right hand is encased in the segmented silver gauntlet – the runes glow softly, and the gaps between plates reveal a faint dark shadow (the corruption) beneath. The contrast between the two hands is stark. Caption below: "The gauntlet is his most distinctive feature, but it is not his only one. There is a way that Alucard holds himself – a stillness, a readiness, a sense that he could explode into motion at any moment – that marks him as dangerous in ways that have nothing to do with the weapon at his hip."

PANEL 6 (Medium, stance – 10% height): Alucard from the side, in a relaxed standing pose. The camera focuses on his posture – weight forward, knees slightly bent, shoulders relaxed but not slouched. His right hand (gauntleted) is at his side, fingers slightly curled. His left hand rests on his sword's hilt. Caption below: "His posture is always slightly forward, weight distributed evenly between his feet, his centre of gravity low. This is the stance of a man who expects to be attacked at any moment, who has trained himself to respond to danger before his conscious mind has even registered its presence. It is not a comfortable stance – it requires constant tension in the legs and core – but Alucard has held it for so long that it has become second nature."

PANEL 7 (Small, voice – 8% height): A close-up on Alucard's mouth and jaw as he speaks (dialogue bubble). The mouth is partially open, the jaw set. The lighting is low-key, emphasising the sharp lines. Speech bubble from Alucard (his own voice, measured, low): "I do not waste words. When I speak, it is because I have something to say. And when I am silent, it is because silence is more useful than noise." Caption below: "His voice is low, measured, each word chosen with care. He does not waste breath on unnecessary speech. This economy of language extends to his interactions with others – he does not offer explanations, does not justify his actions, does not seek approval or validation."

PANEL 8 (Medium, movement – 10% height): A dynamic but subtle panel – Alucard in mid-stride, walking forward, one hand adjusting his coat collar. The motion is fluid, almost predatory. The ink-wash background bleeds into dark sumi strokes behind him, suggesting motion trails. Caption below: "When he does move, it is fast. Not frantic – controlled. Every step, every shift of weight is deliberate. He does not fidget. He does not pace. He simply waits, patient as a glacier, while the world moves around him. And when he decides to act, the world has no time to react."

PANEL 9 (Bottom, wide, cinematic – 12% height): Alucard walking away from the camera, down a path that leads into mist. His greatsword is slung across his back, the skull hilt visible over his right shoulder. The gauntlet's blue glow is the brightest thing in the frame, fading into the fog. The sun is higher now, but the mist holds. Caption in bold handwritten font across the bottom: "He is what he is. Take it or leave it. The demons have learned to fear him. The empire does not know what to do with him. And Alucard – Alucard simply continues. One step at a time. One kill at a time. One day at a time. It is not a philosophy that would satisfy a scholar or a priest. But it is enough for a hunter."

SPEECH BUBBLE STYLE NOTES: Only one speech bubble in this chapter (Panel 7) – thin black outline, white fill with 85% opacity, dark charcoal text. Narrative captions are the primary storytelling device here: rectangular boxes with semi-transparent dark background, white text, placed in corners or along edges, subtle drop shadow. The captions are drawn directly from the autobiography text to emphasize the "anatomy" theme.

