PANEL 1 (Top, establishing wide shot – 15% of image height): The Barren Lands. A vast, grey-brown plain under a perpetually overcast sky. The soil is cracked and lifeless. In the distance, a plume of smoke rises from a small village. Alucard rides his horse Ember in the foreground, small against the enormity of the landscape. He is hunched slightly, his coat pulled tight. His greatsword is visible over his shoulder. The mood is desolate. Caption in top-left corner, typewriter font: "Alucard left the Monastery of Light when he was twenty-two. His departure was not dramatic – no shouted accusations, no burning bridges, no final confrontation. He simply packed his belongings, saddled his horse, and rode south, toward the Barren Lands, toward the Abyss, toward the endless, thankless work of hunting the creatures that had killed his father."

PANEL 2 (Medium, travel montage – 10% height): A horizontal composite panel showing three vignettes of Alucard's wandering: (left) riding through a ruined village, abandoned houses with broken doors; (center) sleeping under a rocky overhang, his sword beside him, his horse standing guard; (right) skinning a rabbit by a small fire, his gauntleted hand carefully holding the knife. No dialogue. Caption below: "He has not looked back. The years since have been a blur of battles, of sleepless nights in ruined fortresses, of tracking demons through terrain that would kill an ordinary man long before the demons got the chance."

PANEL 3 (Large, demon hunt – 20% of image height): A battle scene in a rocky canyon. Alucard faces a pack of three lesser imps – small, twisted creatures with claws and red eyes. He is mid-swing, his sword cutting through one imp while his gauntlet glows, preparing another technique. His horse waits at the canyon mouth. The imps are fast but outmatched. Speech bubble from Alucard (calm, almost bored): "You should have stayed in the Abyss." No reply from imps – only snarls (sound effect "SKREEEE"). Caption at top of panel: "He has fought greater demons and lesser imps, has stood alone against hordes and duelled Abyssal lords in single combat. He has been wounded more times than he can count, has nearly died on at least a dozen occasions."

