PANEL 6 (Small, vertical – 8% height): A close-up on Alucard's gauntlet as he extends his hand toward the fire. The runes are pulsing. Through the gaps in the plates, the dark corruption is visible – black veins crawling. The firelight catches the hairline fractures in the silver. Caption: "The whispers come at night, mostly. They speak in voices he almost recognises – his father's voice, his mother's voice, the voices of soldiers who died in the Second Regiment. They tell him that he is becoming what he hunts."

PANEL 7 (Medium, reputation – 10% height): A tavern interior – dim, smoky. Alucard sits alone at a corner table, a mug of water (not ale) in front of him. In the background, two merchants are whispering, glancing at him. A wanted poster or notice board on the wall has a rough sketch of a man with a gauntlet – not accurate, but close enough. Speech bubble from one merchant (whisper, dashed outline, small): "That's him. Alucard. They say he drinks blood." Second merchant: "I heard he made a pact with a demon." Alucard's face shows no reaction – he simply drinks his water. Caption: "Word travels fast in the Land of Dawn. Alucard the Demon Hunter. Alucard the Crimson Hand. Alucard the Life-Drinker. The last one stung, in a way he had not expected."

PANEL 8 (Large, the hunt continues – 12% height): Dawn. Alucard rides through a grey landscape, his horse walking slowly. In the distance, a demonic glow (green) rises from a cave entrance. He draws his sword. His face is set – not eager, not reluctant. Just resolved. Caption at bottom of panel: "He copes by hunting. When he is tracking a demon, when he is closing in on a kill, the loneliness fades. There is only the chase, the fight, the satisfaction of ending another threat. In those moments, Alucard feels almost alive."

