Tigreal (memory/flashback silhouette): Appears only as a ghostly after-image in one panel – a reminder.

PANEL 1 (Top, establishing wide shot – 12% of image height): A dusty frontier town at the edge of the Barren Lands. Wooden buildings, a central well, a few scraggly trees. The sun is setting, casting long shadows. Alucard rides into town on Ember, his silhouette stark against the orange sky. A few townsfolk stop and stare, then quickly look away. A child points, but a mother pulls the child's hand down. Caption in top-left corner, typewriter font: "Word travels fast in the Land of Dawn, even in places where the only roads are dirt paths and the only messengers are travellers who might or might not be reliable. By the time Alucard had been hunting for five years, his name had acquired a weight that he had not anticipated and did not particularly want."

PANEL 2 (Medium, tavern interior – 15% of image height): A dim, smoke-filled tavern. Alucard sits alone at a corner table, his back to the wall, facing the door. His greatsword is propped beside him. A mug of water sits untouched. In the background, a group of patrons are whispering, glancing at him. The innkeeper wipes a glass, also staring. Speech bubble from a mercenary (whisper, dashed outline, small): "That's him. Alucard. They say he fights like a demon himself." Second mercenary: "I heard his sword drinks blood. He gets stronger the more he kills." Innkeeper (to the mercenaries, low): "Keep your voices down. He's not deaf." Alucard shows no reaction – his face is calm, his eyes scanning the room.

PANEL 3 (Small, close-up – 8% of image height): Close-up on Alucard's face, side-lit by a candle on his table. His icy blue eyes catch the light, giving them an almost supernatural glow. His expression is unreadable – neither angry nor pleased. A faint smirk might be forming at the corner of his mouth, but it's ambiguous. Caption below: "Alucard the Demon Hunter. Alucard the Crimson Hand. Alucard the Life-Drinker. The last one stung, in a way he had not expected. He did not choose to be what he was. He did not ask for the corruption. But the people who whispered his name did not know that."

