Lighting within Action Panels: Each action panel has its own lighting appropriate to the technique (Groundsplitter – natural canyon light; Whirling Smash – overcast fortress light; Fission Wave – dramatic low-key with the blast as the main light source; Passive abilities – forest shadow, blizzard overcast, macro lighting for healing). But Alucard's colors remain consistent.
Ink Wash Elements: The parchment background has sumi ink stains, water rings, and subtle brush strokes in the margins. The action panels have ink splashes at the edges (simulating spilled ink) and sometimes ink-washed backgrounds (e.g., the canyon walls in Groundsplitter can be ink-washed for contrast). The skill icons are rendered with a metallic ink effect (blue and silver pigments).
Character Consistency Enforcement: In every action panel, Alucard must have the exact same face structure (same scars, same grey streaks in hair, same gaunt cheeks, same black veins on neck). His clothing (duster coat, vest, glove, gauntlet, trousers, boots) must be identical – same patches, same cracks, same missing strap. His greatsword must have the same skull hilt (with crack on left eye socket), same bent crossguard tip, same dim blue glow. If the AI struggles with consistency, the prompt should explicitly call out "using the character reference sheet at the top of this prompt" and specify "do not change the outfit between panels."
